  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Wyoming has received $576M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state has 2,393 awards so far, with an average award size of $241K, and obligations are up 15.8% year over year. The Department of the Interior is the largest buyer in the state with $319M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense at $87.7M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $67.6M. Construction-related industries dominate spending: Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction accounts for $247M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $84M. RECORD STEEL AND CONSTRUCTION, INC. and G.S.E. CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INC. lead vendors with $130M and $109M respectively. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations only, so totals are partial for the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers of federal contracts in Wyoming?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior is the largest buyer, obligating $319M. The Department of Defense obligated $87.7M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $67.6M. The Department of Transportation, Department of Agriculture, and General Services Administration follow with $39.8M, $33.8M, and $26.8M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries capture the most federal contract dollars in Wyoming?",
        "body": "Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction is the largest industry, with $247M in obligations. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction are next with $84M and $63.2M. Engineering Services, Automobile and Light Duty Motor Vehicle Manufacturing, and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation account for $30.4M, $26.4M, and $11.8M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
